        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): render identity name in runtime prompt",
        "body": "Restored replacement for #94437 after the fork/head repository was recreated.\n\n## Summary\n- resolve the active `agents.list[].identity.name` into system prompt runtime metadata\n- keep the technical slot id stable as `agent=<id>`\n- render a different configured identity as `agentName=<identity>`\n- preserve current stable cron session rendering while rebasing onto current `main`\n- add focused coverage for prompt params, runtime rendering, and CLI prompt assembly\n\nFixes #81269.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\nRuntime prompt metadata previously only exposed the technical agent slot id, so configured identities could still drift back toward generic ids such as `main`. This PR keeps the stable technical id for existing consumers while exposing the configured display identity separately as `agentName=<identity>`.\n\n## User Impact\nConfigured agent identities can be reflected in the runtime prompt without changing the existing `agent=<id>` contract used for session/debug context.\n\n## Evidence\nLatest local verification on head `18e658ab99afcd703b5672b6054c29ae11e312fd`:\n\n```text\noxfmt --check src/agents/system-prompt.ts src/agents/system-prompt-params.ts src/agents/system-prompt.test.ts src/agents/system-prompt-params.test.ts src/agents/cli-runner/helpers.system-prompt.test.ts\nAll matched files use the correct format.\n\nvitest run src/agents/system-prompt.test.ts src/agents/system-prompt-params.test.ts src/agents/cli-runner/helpers.system-prompt.test.ts --config test/vitest/vitest.agents.config.ts\nTest Files  2 passed (2)\nTests  20 passed (20)\n\nvitest run src/agents/cli-runner/helpers.system-prompt.test.ts\nTest Files  2 passed (2)\nTests  22 passed (22)\n\ngit diff --check\n# no output\n```\n\nLatest-head terminal proof for the final runtime shape:\n\n```text\nnode --import tsx -e 'import { buildSystemPromptParams } from \"./src/agents/system-prompt-params.ts\"; import { buildRuntimeLine } from \"./src/agents/system-prompt.ts\"; const { runtimeInfo } = buildSystemPromptParams({ config: { agents: { list: [{ id: \"Team Ops\", identity: { name: \"Ops Navigator\" } }] } }, agentId: \"team-ops\", runtime: { host: \"host\", os: \"darwin\", arch: \"arm64\", node: process.version, model: \"test-model\" } }); console.log(buildRuntimeLine(runtimeInfo));'\nRuntime: agent=team-ops | agentName=Ops Navigator | host=host | os=darwin (arm64) | node=v25.9.0 | model=test-model | thinking=off\n```\n\nObserved result after fix: The technical id remains in `agent=team-ops`; the configured identity is rendered as `agentName=Ops Navigator` only when it differs from the id. Focused tests also cover identity-name resolution, prompt rendering, and CLI prompt assembly.\n\n## Not Tested\nA live agent conversation was not started in this environment; the focused prompt construction and CLI assembly paths exercise the affected runtime prompt output.\n\n---\nReopened after active-PR limit cleanup. Supersedes closed PR #94397.\n",
